# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GTS Algo Research — CONSERVATIVE MUMBAI EC2 PROFILE (ap-south-1)
#
# Copy to .env and edit the values marked EDIT. See docs/MUMBAI_EC2_PROFILE.md for
# the reasoning behind every number and docs/CONFIGURATION.md for the full list.
#
# REAL TRADING IS DISABLED IN THIS FILE. Two independent switches must BOTH be set
# before any real order can be placed, and BOX_EXECUTION_MODE=live is REJECTED AT
# BOOT unless BOX_LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED=true (src/box/config.ts loadBoxConfig) — so
# a single stray variable cannot arm live trading.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS NOT: it contains NO secret, NO token and NO approved capital
# budget. Every number here is a conservative starting default OR a clearly-marked
# placeholder the operator must set. It is NOT proof any trade will fill or profit.
#
# Values marked (default) equal the shipped code default; they are written out
# anyway so the posture is explicit rather than inherited. Confirm the EFFECTIVE
# resolved values at runtime with:  node dist/box/effectiveConfig.js
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── EXECUTION MODE: real trading DISABLED ────────────────────────────────────
BOX_EXECUTION_MODE=paper_latency          # (default) flip to `live` only when supervised + armed
BOX_LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED=false            # (default) deployment kill switch — the second gate
BOX_SHADOW_MODE_ENABLED=false             # (default) shadow cannot ever place an order
BOX_PAPER_EXECUTION_PROFILE=standard      # (default) never `stress` near real money (rejected in live)

# ── SIZE: one lot per leg, one active box, one box per underlying ────────────
BOX_LIVE_MAX_OPEN_BOXES=1                  # (default) one active box
BOX_LIVE_MAX_CONCURRENT_EXECUTIONS=1      # (default) one execution pipeline at a time
BOX_ONE_ACTIVE_BOX_PER_UNDERLYING=true    # ON (code default is false) — one box per underlying
BOX_SESSION_MAX_COMPLETED_TRADES=1        # EXPLICITLY ARM a one-completed-box session (default 0=unlimited)
BOX_MAX_CONCURRENT_PER_UNDERLYING=1       # tighten from default 2 for the first sessions

# ── ATTEMPT CEILING — THE OTHER HALF OF "ONE TRADE" ──────────────────────────
# THIS PROFILE PREVIOUSLY OMITTED IT, AND THE OMISSION WAS THE HOLE.
# BOX_SESSION_MAX_COMPLETED_TRADES=1 bounds SUCCESS, not RISK-TAKING: a cycle is
# consumed only when a full four-leg Box is ESTABLISHED. An attempt that submits
# legs, partially fills and is unwound establishes nothing and therefore spends NO
# cycle — so with the attempt ceiling left at its default of 0 (UNLIMITED), a trial
# "configured for one trade" could submit orders indefinitely provided no attempt
# ever completed a Box. That is the opposite of a supervised one-lot trial.
#
# ONE attempt for the FIRST supervised session. Consumed at ADMISSION, before any
# broker POST, and durable — a restart does not hand it back. Practical submission
# ceiling is therefore 4 legs (plus any protective unwind/recovery orders, which are
# deliberately NOT counted, because refusing to reduce exposure is never safer).
BOX_SESSION_MAX_ENTRY_ATTEMPTS=1          # EXPLICIT one-attempt ceiling (default 0=UNLIMITED)
#
# RE-ARMING IS REQUIRED TO CHANGE IT. Both ceilings are SNAPSHOTTED INTO THE ARMED
# SESSION ROW at arm time (migrations/010_session_entry_attempts.sql), so an already
# armed session keeps the budget it was armed under. Editing this file and restarting
# does NOT change a live session's budget. To change it: go FLAT (no open box, no
# residual leg, no recovery), then deliberately DISARM and RE-ARM. Confirm both the
# configured and the armed values afterwards — they are reported separately:
#   GET /api/box/status → effective_config.session_max_entry_attempts   (CONFIGURED)
#                       → session.max_entry_attempts                   (ARMED snapshot)
#                       → session.remaining_entry_attempts             (null = unbounded)
# If those two disagree, the armed session is authoritative.

# ── ENTRY TRANSPORT CONCURRENCY ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keep 1. The offline benchmark shows 2 and 4 do not materially help: the broker
# pacing floor plus the hedge-first dependency binds. Concurrency 4 does NOT make
# four-leg execution atomic.
BOX_LIVE_ENTRY_SUBMIT_CONCURRENCY=1       # (default; min 1, max 4)

# ── QUANTITY ENVELOPE (one lot; sized so a single lot cannot exceed it) ──────
BOX_LIVE_MAX_OPEN_LEG_QUANTITY=100        # (default) per-leg absolute quantity ceiling
BOX_LIVE_MAX_GROSS_OPEN_LEG_QUANTITY=400  # (default) sum of |open leg quantities|

# ── CAPITAL: GROSS ORDER NOTIONAL — PLACEHOLDER, not margin / peak / max loss ─
# Code default is 0 = DISABLED. The value below is a PLACEHOLDER you MUST set to
# your own approved figure before going live. It is GROSS option-order notional,
# NOT broker margin, NOT peak legging capital, NOT maximum loss. See
# docs/ECONOMIC_ADMISSION.md. Do NOT treat this example number as an approved budget.
BOX_LIVE_MAX_BOX_CAPITAL_RUPEES=100000    # EDIT: placeholder — set your approved cap

# ── ECONOMIC ADMISSION: funds / COMPLETE margin / STAGE funding (entry only) ──
# All three OFF by code default. All three ON here: this profile now REQUIRES usable
# funds AND a defensible execution-stage funding requirement. Neither ever blocks
# protective reduction — exits, cancellation and residual flattening are ungated.
#
# WHY THIS CHANGED. Funds-cover used to be satisfiable WITHOUT any margin figure: when
# no broker margin was usable, the check fell back to the worst-case GROSS OPTION
# PREMIUM of the BUY legs. Gross premium does not bound the margin a SHORT option
# attracts — a box's premium outlay can be a small fraction of it — so the gate could
# pass on a number that had nothing to do with the requirement. That fallback is gone:
# with no usable stage requirement and no usable broker margin, admission now refuses
# `metric_incomplete` instead of substituting premium.
#
# Margin evidence is now REQUIRED, and "evidence" now means COMPLETE evidence. The Dhan
# per-leg fallback used to return a sum over however many legs happened to answer — a
# 1-of-4 sum was accepted as a basket margin — so every requested leg must now resolve
# and return a structurally valid figure, or the basket is unusable for admission.
BOX_LIVE_REQUIRE_FUNDS_COVER=true         # ON (code default false)
BOX_LIVE_REQUIRE_MARGIN_EVIDENCE=true     # ON (code default false) — COMPLETE broker margin required
BOX_LIVE_REQUIRE_STAGE_FUNDING=true       # ON (code default false) — read BROKER SUPPORT below
BOX_LIVE_FUNDS_FRESHNESS_MAX_AGE_MS=5000  # (default) funds older than this are not "fresh"
BOX_LIVE_MARGIN_FRESHNESS_MAX_AGE_MS=5000 # (default)
BOX_LIVE_EVIDENCE_READ_TIMEOUT_MS=2500    # (default) hard per-read deadline; a stalled broker
                                          # endpoint cannot hold admission open
BOX_LIVE_EVIDENCE_CONCURRENT_READS=false  # (default) read funds and margin serially
#
# NOTE ON THE THREE GATES ABOVE: they are NOT independent. STAGE_FUNDING implies BOTH
# FUNDS_COVER and MARGIN_EVIDENCE — a per-stage requirement that is never compared
# against money would be a gate in name only. The EFFECTIVE values are published at
# /api/box/status -> economic_admission.funding_readiness.gates.

# ── RECOVERY RESERVE — YOU MUST SIZE THIS; THERE IS NO SAFE DEFAULT ──────────
# Funds held back so a RECOVERY action (cancel, unwind, complete) is not blocked for
# want of money. It is an additive component of the binding requirement, so raising it
# makes entry stricter. 0 reserves NOTHING.
#
# This project does NOT compute a value for you and 0 must not be read as adequate.
# To size it, decide for YOUR account and instruments:
#   1. the worst intermediate state this deployment can reach (one partially filled box
#      at BOX_LIVE_MAX_OPEN_BOXES and your lot size);
#   2. the margin the broker would demand to COMPLETE that box from there — the
#      completing leg is a real order with its own margin, not free;
#   3. the cost of UNWINDING the filled legs instead, including charges and realistic
#      adverse slippage;
#   4. your broker's intraday margin-call / auto-square-off behaviour, which can demand
#      funds before either action finishes.
# Set the reserve to max(2, 3) plus a buffer for (4). See
# docs/ECONOMIC_ADMISSION.md "Sizing the recovery reserve".
BOX_LIVE_RECOVERY_RESERVE_RUPEES=0        # (default) EDIT: 0 reserves nothing

# ── BROKER SUPPORT FOR STAGE FUNDING — READ BEFORE ARMING ────────────────────
# Stage funding asks a specific question: can the account fund the WORST INTERMEDIATE
# POINT of the four-leg sequence? While hedges are still going out the completed-basket
# spread benefit does not exist yet, so the FINAL hedged margin is NOT sufficient
# evidence for the intermediate stages. In Zerodha's own published basket example the
# two figures differ by roughly 2.8x.
#
#   ZERODHA — SUPPORTED. Kite's basket-margin API documents `data.initial.total` as the
#   margin required to EXECUTE the orders and `data.final.total` as the margin WITH the
#   spread benefit. The stage model consumes both, and each block's PRESENCE is tracked
#   separately from its value, so a block Zerodha did not send is UNKNOWN, not ₹0.
#
#   DHAN — NOT ESTABLISHED. Dhan publishes no field documented as an execute-the-orders
#   margin. `spanMargin` is a COMPONENT of the requirement, not a statement about any
#   intermediate point of the sequence, and it was previously mapped onto `initial`
#   (with `?? 0`, so an ABSENT span became an established requirement of ₹0 and the
#   stage requirement collapsed to the gross premium). It is now reported UNKNOWN.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, STATED PLAINLY: with DHAN active and this profile as written, live entry
# is BLOCKED with `funding_stage_unknown`. That is intended — the gate is not weakened
# to let Dhan through. Confirm before arming:
#   node dist/box/effectiveConfig.js | grep BOX_LIVE_   # what is ACTUALLY in force
#   GET /api/box/status → economic_admission.funding_readiness.status
#        must read `verified` (or `not_evaluated` before the first candidate),
#        NEVER `checks_disabled` — that value means nothing was checked at all.
#   GET /api/box/status → operational_readiness.entry.reasons
#        a funding refusal appears here as a `funding_*` entry-scoped blocker; it never
#        blocks exits, reductions or protective cancellation.
#   GET /api/box/status → economic_admission.reasons and .detail
# To run the first supervised trial on DHAN, FIRST resolve the broker semantics (see
# docs/BROKER_LIMITS.md "TO RESOLVE") or implement a documented per-stage margin
# calculation. Do NOT set BOX_LIVE_REQUIRE_STAGE_FUNDING=false to get past it: that
# converts a clear blocked status into an unbounded intermediate-funding assumption.

# ── LOSS BREAKER — stops NEW entries; NOT a guaranteed maximum loss ──────────
BOX_LIVE_DAILY_LOSS_LIMIT=5000            # (default) "stop digging", not a loss cap
BOX_LIVE_REJECT_LIMIT=3                   # (default) reject count that trips the breaker
BOX_LIVE_CONSECUTIVE_FAILURE_LIMIT=3      # (default)

# ── FRESHNESS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BOX_QUOTE_MAX_AGE_MS=15000                # (default) how long an UNCHANGED book stays valid
BOX_FEED_MAX_AGE_MS=5000                  # (default) whole-universe feed liveness
BOX_UNDERLYING_MAX_AGE_MS=10000           # (default) underlying spot age for ATM centring

# ── FOUR-LEG COHERENCE (whole-second exchange stamps — no sub-second gate) ───
# RECEIVE-time dispersion is the ALWAYS-available gate: Dhan publishes NO order-book
# timestamp, and Kite's is 1-second granular. This is the primary LIVE gate.
BOX_MAX_CROSS_LEG_RECEIVE_DISPERSION_MS=500        # (default)
# EXCHANGE-time dispersion applies only when EVERY leg carries a real book timestamp.
# PRECISION TRAP: Kite's stamp is whole SECONDS, so any value <1000 could reject
# coherent books on quantisation alone. Code default is 250 (BELOW Kite precision),
# raised here to 1000 so a Zerodha-only run does not self-reject on rounding.
BOX_MAX_CROSS_LEG_EXCHANGE_DISPERSION_MS=1000
BOX_MAX_RECEIVE_TO_EXCHANGE_DELAY_MS=5000          # (default) tolerates coarse stamps + feed lag
# In LIVE a 0 dispersion limit is IMPOSSIBLE-TO-SATISFY, not a silent bypass. Keep
# false so an unconfigured operator can never accidentally lose cross-leg enforcement.
BOX_COHERENCE_ZERO_DISPERSION_DISABLES_IN_LIVE=false   # (default)

# ── BOUNDED LIFECYCLE DEADLINES ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# One end-to-end budget per mutation, started BEFORE queue admission (deadline.ts),
# plus per-phase timeouts. Conservative values: fail promptly rather than hang a leg.
BOX_LIVE_ORDER_MUTATION_DEADLINE_MS=4000  # (default) absolute per-mutation budget
BOX_LIVE_HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS=5000             # (default)
BOX_LIVE_ACK_TIMEOUT_MS=3000              # (default)
BOX_LIVE_WORKING_TIMEOUT_MS=30000         # (default)
BOX_LIVE_PARTIAL_TIMEOUT_MS=10000         # (default)
BOX_LIVE_CANCEL_TIMEOUT_MS=5000           # (default)
BOX_LIVE_MAX_MODIFICATIONS=2              # (default)
BOX_LIVE_MAX_CHASE_TICKS=2                # (default) marketable-limit chase band

# ── RATE BUDGET / PACING (one app-owned budget per broker account) ───────────
# 0 = derive the ORDER-MUTATION interval from the broker's published limit (clamped
# UP to the broker floor; never zero). The general poll cadence is separate.
BOX_LIVE_BROKER_ORDER_MIN_INTERVAL_MS=0   # (default) derive from broker floor
BOX_LIVE_BROKER_MIN_INTERVAL_MS=250       # (default) general polls / lists / margins / health
BOX_LIVE_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_MS=60000      # (default) low-frequency broker reconciliation
BOX_LIVE_FEED_RECONNECT_WARMUP_MS=5000    # (default) quiet period after a feed reconnect before entry

# ── ORDER-EVENT INGESTION BACKPRESSURE (never-drop threshold, NOT a cap) ─────
# Above this many queued raw order-event frames the pipeline reports OVERLOAD:
# it BLOCKS new entry and triggers reconciliation while still delivering every
# event. Data is never dropped — a missing order event is never a zero fill.
BOX_ORDER_EVENT_QUEUE_PRESSURE=512        # (default)

# ── RESERVATIONS (contract exclusion) ────────────────────────────────────────
BOX_DURABLE_RESERVATIONS_ENABLED=true     # (default) cross-process exclusion via the DB
BOX_RESERVATION_REQUIRE_DURABLE=false     # (default) single PM2 fork; set true for multi-worker
BOX_INSTRUMENT_LOCK_TTL_MS=5000           # (default) crash-recovery lease bound
BOX_EXECUTION_COORDINATOR_ENABLED=true    # (default) do not disable while trading
BOX_INTERNAL_NETTING_ENABLED=false        # (default) MUST stay off until virtual ownership exists

# ── ENVIRONMENT DIAGNOSTICS (event-loop lag measured in executionEnvironment.ts) ─
BOX_EXECUTION_EVENT_LOOP_METRICS_ENABLED=true   # (default) fail-open; never affects trading
BOX_EXECUTION_TIMING_METRICS_ENABLED=true       # (default) fail-open latency calibration
BOX_DEPLOYMENT_REGION=mumbai              # stamp calibration datasets; NEVER auto-detected

# ── ENTRY GATE ECONOMICS (the two runtime-tunable numbers) ───────────────────
BOX_MIN_EXPECTED_NET_PROFIT=1200          # (default) THE gate: expected net profit after every cost
BOX_SAFETY_BUFFER=150                     # (default) risk allowance inside the net figure

# ── ORDER-UPDATE STREAMS vs THE MARKET-DATA FEED ───────────────────────
# TWO DIFFERENT CONCERNS. Conflating them is a real hazard, and the status payload
# carries a dedicated flag saying so (`order_stream.market_data_health_is_not_order_
# stream_health: true`). Verified against the code, not the docs:
#
#   MARKET-DATA feed  — quotes/depth for the scanner. Zerodha: wss://ws.kite.trade
#     (BINARY frames, src/ticker.ts). Dhan: wss://api-feed.dhan.co
#     (src/brokers/dhan/feed.ts). Reported under `market_data_*` / `feed_*` /
#     `authenticated` — note that `authenticated` is MARKET-DATA auth, nothing to do
#     with order updates.
#   ORDER-UPDATE stream — fill/state notifications for OUR OWN orders. Reported ONLY
#     under `order_stream`. These two switches control it.
#
#   TRANSPORT DETAIL WORTH KNOWING: Zerodha has NO separate order socket and no HTTP
#   webhook receiver in this build — order updates arrive as TEXT frames on the SAME
#   Kite quote socket that carries the binary ticks. So for Zerodha a healthy
#   market-data socket is a PRE-REQUISITE for order updates but still does not mean
#   they are being CONSUMED: ZERODHA_ORDER_STREAM_ENABLED gates the observation path
#   itself, and with it false the frame is dropped before it is even parsed.
#   Dhan is the opposite shape — a genuinely separate socket
#   (wss://api-order-update.dhan.co).
#
# THIS PROFILE IS REST-ONLY, DELIBERATELY, AND THAT MODE IS SUPPORTED.
# Both switches are OFF, so fills are observed by BOUNDED REST RECONCILIATION. That
# path is NOT conditional on these flags: the order manager starts a periodic
# reconcile timer in every live deployment at BOX_LIVE_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_MS (60s
# here, floored at 5s in code), and it also reconciles targeted orders on demand.
# LATENCY IMPLICATION, stated honestly: fill observation is as late as that cadence,
# so a partial fill can sit unobserved for up to the reconcile interval, and the
# hedge-coverage ledger only advances on a CONFIRMED fill. For a supervised
# one-attempt trial with an operator watching, that is an acceptable trade for one
# fewer moving part. Enabling the streams makes the same truth arrive sooner; it does
# not replace REST, which remains the authority of record either way.
#
# BEFORE ENABLING EITHER — deliberately, one broker at a time, then re-verify:
#   1. `/api/box/status → order_stream.brokers[]` for that broker must show
#      `wiring: "armed"` (NOT merely `gate_enabled: true`) and
#      `fills_observed_by: "stream_primary_rest_reconcile"`. While
#      `fills_observed_by` still reads `rest_polling_only`, the stream is not being
#      used for fills no matter what the socket is doing.
#   2. ACCOUNT/SESSION BINDING: the stream must belong to the same account the orders
#      are placed from. Nothing in the payload proves this beyond `health.lastEventAt`
#      advancing for orders you actually sent — confirm an event arrived for a known
#      client_order_id before trusting it.
#   3. RECONNECT RECONCILIATION: a reconnect puts the consumer in RECONCILING and NEW
#      ENTRY IS REFUSED until a REST sweep returns `synchronized: true` (readiness
#      blocker `order_stream_lifecycle`). This is a real, checked verdict with an
#      epoch guard and backoff — not a timer. It is a DIFFERENT bar from the
#      market-data reconnect quiet period (BOX_LIVE_FEED_RECONNECT_WARMUP_MS), which
#      is purely time-based and involves no reconciliation.
#   4. Keep REST reconciliation ON regardless. Neither broker promises event REPLAY
#      across a disconnect, so a stream alone cannot be trusted to have delivered
#      every fill.
#
# WHAT MUST NOT BE CLAIMED — verified limitations, not caution for its own sake:
#   * AN OPEN DHAN SOCKET IS NOT PROOF OF ORDER-STREAM AUTHENTICATION. The Dhan
#     protocol publishes no authentication response frame, so the transport reports
#     `authorised: true` as soon as the login frame has been WRITTEN
#     (src/brokers/dhan/orderFeed.ts). A rejected auth only shows up later as a close
#     code. The code is honest about this internally — it records the evidence as
#     `login_submitted`, which does NOT establish a session — but that means
#     `order_stream.health.authorised === true` MUST NOT be read as "authenticated for
#     this account". The load-bearing signal is `lifecycle: "READY"`, reachable only
#     after a successful REST sweep, plus a recent `health.lastEventAt`.
#   * NO CLAIM OF ZERO OUTAGES OR GUARANTEED FILL UPDATES is made in either mode. A
#     MISSING order event is never read as a zero fill: the event queue is never-drop,
#     a backlog BLOCKS new entry and forces reconciliation
#     (BOX_ORDER_EVENT_QUEUE_PRESSURE above), and a terminal status label that arrives
#     WITHOUT a cumulative filled quantity is refused as unproven and reconciled
#     rather than accounted as zero.
ZERODHA_ORDER_STREAM_ENABLED=false        # (default) text-frame order updates NOT consumed — fills via REST polling only
DHAN_ORDER_STREAM_ENABLED=false           # (default) dedicated Dhan order socket not opened — fills via REST polling only

# ── POSTGRESQL — authoritative operational state, same EC2 host ──────────────
# Do NOT set synchronous_commit=off anywhere: durability before transport is
# load-bearing (src/pg/pool.ts). Pool acquisition is bounded (connectionTimeoutMillis).
DATABASE_URL=postgres:///strikedge        # Unix socket on the same host (no password on the wire)
PG_POOL_MAX=10                            # (default) generous for a single-process app
PG_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS=5000              # (default) per-connection; a wedged statement fails, not hangs
PG_LOCK_TIMEOUT_MS=2000                   # (default)
PG_MIGRATE_ON_BOOT=true                   # (default) false = boot refuses on a stale schema
PG_APPLICATION_NAME=gts                   # (default) names the deployment in pg_stat_activity

# ── MongoDB Atlas — ASYNCHRONOUS projection only, never awaited on the order path ─
MONGODB_URI=                              # EDIT: mongodb+srv://… (reporting/history only)

# ── APPLICATION (see src/config.ts) ──────────────────────────────────────────
NODE_ENV=production
APP_TIMEZONE=Asia/Kolkata                 # (default) every trading-day decision is IST; rejected otherwise
FRONTEND_URL=                             # EDIT: exact https origin (CORS is exact-origin, never *)
PORT=3001                                 # (default)
SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS=20000                 # (default)

# ── OPERATIONAL PRECONDITIONS (NOT enforceable in code — verify by hand) ─────
# 1. STATIC EGRESS IP: attach an Elastic IP (or NAT with a fixed EIP) and register
#    that ONE address with BOTH brokers. Dhan additionally requires a DECLARED
#    static IP; the app verifies via registry.ts dhanStaticIpReady/verifyDhanStaticIp
#    and blocks Dhan live placement until it is ready. Set DHAN_STATIC_IP_EXPECTED=true
#    only once the address is actually registered in the Dhan console.
#    DHAN_STATIC_IP_EXPECTED=true                # EDIT: set ONLY after registering the IP
# 2. CLOCK SYNC: chrony against Amazon Time Sync (169.254.169.123); verify
#    `chronyc tracking` shows offset well under 50 ms. Audit timestamps depend on it.
# 3. CALSPREAD OFF: the predecessor codebase Box execution MUST be disabled before arming GTS Algo Research
#    live against a shared broker account. Rate budgets and reservations are
#    per-application; two systems on one account cannot see each other. Verify the
#    the predecessor codebase process is stopped and holds no open box before cutover (see
#    docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §the predecessor codebase cutover).
